WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
Four printed slips.

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.460
Four spellings of the same word.

3
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:09.450
In 1490, the printer Caxton complained
that he couldn't even settle how to write

4
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.130
the word for eggs.

5
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.870
Today, only one of those
four spellings survives.

6
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.110
So who decided how
English should be spelled?

7
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.240
And why did anyone listen?

8
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:24.130
In this mission, you'll ask what the
printing press had to do with it.

9
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.260
You'll weigh up a famous dictionary.

10
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:28.490
Did it really settle everything?

11
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.970
And you'll find that grammar has changed,

12
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.520
as well as spelling.

13
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.010
Your mission: find out who
decided, and why anyone listened.
